Subject: [PATCH] 5052: ask and request threads get their short titles when
 they are created
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Short titles were written only where the model names a conversation. Ask and
request threads are titled by code when they are created, so they never got
one, and the one-off backfill could not reach threads opened after it. Their
title showed cut off with „…" in the list and the chat header (Giorgi's
example is an ask thread). shortTitlesForNewThread asks for them as each such
thread is created; same text and model as every other short title (4919).
FOR_FRONTEND: show short_title in the list and the header.

